%% Each box row goes to one investor; the amount is the total capital of the chosen rows (boxes × Standard Cost per box), so the minimum contribution is
%% one row. Connector A continues on part 2. The fork runs payment and contract in parallel, as in code: the wizard goes disclosure → amount → contract →
%% VietQR → done, the contract can be drafted while the reservation holds, and signing does not block payment; the join is on part 3. Connectors B
%% (contract fully signed), C (payment received in time) and D (late transfer to refund) continue on part 3. An unpaid reservation simply expires after
%% 30 minutes (expiry job): rows released, contract voided. The Batch opens when the minimum viable capital is reached AND the pre-order ratio is at
%% least the minimum set by the Administrator; otherwise it is cancelled and investors and every depositing Customer are refunded, cancelled pre-orders
%% included. Between the minimum and the target only the boxes of funded rows are stocked, and settlement deducts the locked Standard Cost of those boxes
%% only. The join waits for both branches of part 2: stocking needs the capital closed and every contract FullySigned (Figure 4.8). Both refund paths end
%% the activity, so a contract still waiting at the join is voided. Traceability: UC02, UC09, UC11, UC10, UC14, UC12, UC40, funding close job (TP1
%% Thiện). Exception branches: eKYC rejected; transfer after the 30-minute hold (refunded); minimum viable capital not reached or pre-orders below the
%% minimum ratio → Batch cancelled, refunds. «planned» in v1.4: box-row choice and row hold (one investor per row), keeping only the boxes of funded
%% rows, price per kg and floor price on the offering, the minimum pre-order ratio in the funding-close condition (the code closes on minimum viable
%% capital only) and refunds of Customer deposits. One payment per contribution, no instalments; UC15 Upload Offline-Signed Contract (Administrator)
%% replaces the two e-signatures for paper signing (not drawn). Removed in v1.4 (still in code): UC13 Register Offtake Commitment. States: contribution
%% Reserved → Confirmed / Expired / Refunded (Figure 4.9); row allocation Held → Allocated / Released «planned»; contract Draft → OperatorSigned →
%% FullySigned / Void (4.10); payment request Pending → Paid / Expired (4.11); refund instruction Created → Succeeded / Failed (4.12); Batch Funding →
%% capital closed / Cancelled (4.8). Design decisions of 05/11/2026 applied here were confirmed by the lead.
